message: "If you use this methodology, please cite it as below."
title: "AICD: Artificial Intelligence Centered Development"
authors:
  - family-names: "Ngatcha Sahane"
    given-names: "Rachid Alim"
version: "0.3"
date-released: "2026-09-30" # The document gives only the month, September 2026, so the last day of that month is used.
url: "https://github.com/rachidsahane/AICD-METHODOLOGY"
repository-code: "https://github.com/rachidsahane/AICD-METHODOLOGY"
license: CC-BY-4.0
keywords:
  - "software development methodology"
  - "AI agents"
  - "agentic engineering"
  - "spec-driven development"
  - "software engineering"
abstract: >-
  AICD is a software development methodology in which a complete development
  team is reproduced with AI agents, each with its own role and its own
  context, supervised by a small team of experienced human engineers who
  specify, verify, decide and monitor. The agents build, test, operate and
  document the software from written specifications, while the humans never
  write production code or test code and remain accountable for the
  specification, the control points and the decisions.
